1
00:00:51,511 --> 00:00:55,138
[Episode 4. Too Easy or Utterly Impossible]

2
00:00:55,138 --> 00:00:56,604
Jin, let's hear it.

3
00:00:58,099 --> 00:01:01,186
<i>Hello, I'm Carol.</i>

4
00:01:01,186 --> 00:01:03,388
<i>Nice to meet you.</i>

5
00:01:04,147 --> 00:01:07,194
<i>Well? Is this voice no good either?</i>

6
00:01:08,535 --> 00:01:13,631
<i>So your tastes, even your favorite colors...
You let other people choose for you?</i>

7
00:01:13,631 --> 00:01:15,241
By the way, Jin,

8
00:01:15,241 --> 00:01:17,881
what do you think her favorite color is?

9
00:01:17,881 --> 00:01:19,656
<i>Her favorite color?</i>

10
00:01:33,134 --> 00:01:36,410
I bet he's cooped up in there again.

11
00:01:36,410 --> 00:01:39,715
If he's going to make me work late,
he should at least feed me.

12
00:01:45,522 --> 00:01:47,363
How can I not hear a thing?

13
00:01:55,449 --> 00:01:57,828
Right. It's soundproofed.

14
00:02:01,704 --> 00:02:02,872
Hello?

15
00:02:02,872 --> 00:02:04,082
Hey.

16
00:02:04,749 --> 00:02:06,501
Working late again? Don't tell me.

17
00:02:06,501 --> 00:02:07,794
Yeah.

18
00:02:07,794 --> 00:02:10,547
Can I sleep at the club tonight?

19
00:02:10,547 --> 00:02:12,757
Why? What's going on?

20
00:02:12,757 --> 00:02:15,377
<i>I was a little late for curfew last night,</i>

21
00:02:15,377 --> 00:02:19,305
and my dad came at me with the clippers.

22
00:02:19,305 --> 00:02:21,808
I'm not in high school anymore.

23
00:02:21,808 --> 00:02:25,311
This is my chance to show him
that I'm a real adult

24
00:02:25,311 --> 00:02:28,022
who can make my own choices and act on them.

25
00:02:28,022 --> 00:02:30,400
So you want to sleep at the club?

26
00:02:30,400 --> 00:02:32,026
Just sleep at my place.

27
00:02:32,026 --> 00:02:33,653
I'll sleep at the club instead.

28
00:02:33,653 --> 00:02:36,239
Sleep at your place?

29
00:02:36,239 --> 00:02:41,182
Dong Woo, this is why you're our leader.

30
00:02:42,328 --> 00:02:43,489
Thanks.

31
00:02:46,995 --> 00:02:48,175
Oh, my!

32
00:02:52,547 --> 00:02:54,007
Why on earth

33
00:02:54,007 --> 00:02:56,259
are you eavesdropping on my call?

34
00:02:56,259 --> 00:02:58,511
Who's eavesdropping?

35
00:02:58,511 --> 00:03:00,305
You're the one talking so loud.

36
00:03:00,305 --> 00:03:02,140
Was I that loud?

37
00:03:02,140 --> 00:03:04,684
I thought it was soundproof.

38
00:03:04,684 --> 00:03:06,060
Go home tonight.

39
00:03:06,060 --> 00:03:08,062
Your father's the only one to trust.

40
00:03:08,062 --> 00:03:11,482
So even if he shaves your head, sleep at home.

41
00:03:15,653 --> 00:03:17,196
You're going home, right?

42
00:03:21,159 --> 00:03:22,744
Not telling.

43
00:03:41,179 --> 00:03:42,513
<i>Where are you?</i>

44
00:03:42,513 --> 00:03:44,307
Why are you picking up?

45
00:03:44,307 --> 00:03:45,725
Are you with Jin Woo?

46
00:03:45,725 --> 00:03:47,527
Why are you looking for him?

47
00:03:47,527 --> 00:03:50,229
And you stayed out all night.
Have you lost your mind?

48
00:03:50,229 --> 00:03:52,766
I'm perfectly sane. That's why I need him.

49
00:03:52,766 --> 00:03:55,554
If I go home alone, I'm dead.

50
00:03:57,111 --> 00:03:59,322
Eun Chae, where are you?

51
00:03:59,322 --> 00:04:01,491
We're arriving at Father's house now.

52
00:04:01,491 --> 00:04:02,825
Really?

53
00:04:02,825 --> 00:04:05,119
Then I'll wait outside.

54
00:04:05,119 --> 00:04:06,746
<i>Okay, got it.</i>

55
00:04:06,746 --> 00:04:08,116
Okay.

56
00:04:17,382 --> 00:04:19,384
<i>Sleep at your place?</i>

57
00:04:19,384 --> 00:04:22,829
<i>Dong Woo.</i>

58
00:04:22,829 --> 00:04:24,444
Don't tell me...

59
00:04:32,772 --> 00:04:34,787
What am I doing here?

60
00:04:51,249 --> 00:04:53,084
- It's fine.
- What do you mean?

61
00:04:53,084 --> 00:04:54,502
- Hey!
- Eun Chae.

62
00:04:54,502 --> 00:04:55,796
Get over here, now.

63
00:04:57,807 --> 00:04:58,994
- Stop.
- Hopeless.

64
00:04:58,994 --> 00:05:00,383
- Get over here.
- Let's go.

65
00:05:00,383 --> 00:05:02,593
- Where did you sleep?
- It really hurts.

66
00:05:02,593 --> 00:05:04,137
Where did you sleep?

67
00:05:04,137 --> 00:05:07,640
That's not the point right now.
Dad's going to kill me.

68
00:05:07,640 --> 00:05:09,017
Just come on. Hurry.

69
00:05:09,017 --> 00:05:11,575
You're going to beat me to death at this rate.

70
00:05:14,897 --> 00:05:18,192
My back is going to give out.

71
00:05:25,533 --> 00:05:26,951
Father.

72
00:05:26,951 --> 00:05:28,036
Dad.

73
00:05:28,036 --> 00:05:30,515
- You're here.
- Were you resting?

74
00:05:34,417 --> 00:05:37,378
You little brat!
How dare you stay out all night?

75
00:05:37,378 --> 00:05:39,912
You were holding the clippers, so I ran away.

76
00:05:39,912 --> 00:05:43,593
- How dare you talk back to me?
- Father, please calm down.

77
00:05:43,593 --> 00:05:46,054
She's a grown woman. You can't shave her head.

78
00:05:46,054 --> 00:05:49,307
Yeah, Dad. Look at her face.

79
00:05:49,307 --> 00:05:51,976
Her hair is the only thing
that makes her look decent.

80
00:05:51,976 --> 00:05:53,269
That's not true.

81
00:05:53,269 --> 00:05:55,229
Mom said I have a nicely shaped head.

82
00:05:55,229 --> 00:05:59,025
Mom was just being nice
because you get hurt so easily.

83
00:05:59,025 --> 00:06:00,943
- It's true.
- Wait,

84
00:06:00,943 --> 00:06:02,445
why play favorites, Dad?

85
00:06:02,445 --> 00:06:05,239
You never threatened to shave Eun Seo's!

86
00:06:05,239 --> 00:06:08,201
Dad! Just shave her head already!

87
00:06:08,201 --> 00:06:09,970
Both of you, be quiet!

88
00:06:17,085 --> 00:06:20,347
Honey, I'm sorry.

89
00:06:20,347 --> 00:06:23,018
I must have raised them wrong.

90
00:06:25,218 --> 00:06:29,382
I guess my hair's time is up, too.

91
00:06:30,425 --> 00:06:32,372
- I'll just shave mine.
- Dad.

92
00:06:32,372 --> 00:06:34,872
- Father!
- Dad!

93
00:06:36,062 --> 00:06:38,606
Seriously, why are you doing this?

94
00:06:38,606 --> 00:06:40,066
- Please!
- Don't do it!

95
00:06:40,066 --> 00:06:43,261
Please, Father. Please stop, please!

96
00:06:47,031 --> 00:06:49,575
This year's financials for Seheon Hotel Resort.

97
00:06:49,575 --> 00:06:51,994
Reviewing them first will help in the meeting.

98
00:06:51,994 --> 00:06:56,624
Why does he want me handling that, too?

99
00:06:56,624 --> 00:07:00,294
The chairman plans to expand
the resort business this year.

100
00:07:00,294 --> 00:07:04,549
I believe he wants you to take control of it.

101
00:07:04,549 --> 00:07:07,416
So again, why should I...

102
00:07:17,019 --> 00:07:19,438
After the resort team meeting this afternoon,

103
00:07:19,438 --> 00:07:22,942
you have dinner with directors
of the hotel we're looking to buy.

104
00:07:22,942 --> 00:07:26,654
You'll probably have to go straight home
from your meetings today.

105
00:07:26,654 --> 00:07:27,947
What about the agency?

106
00:07:27,947 --> 00:07:30,158
I've moved all your Wednesday meetings.

107
00:07:30,158 --> 00:07:32,325
- It's Wednesday today?
- Yes.

108
00:07:45,840 --> 00:07:47,675
Yes, Mr. Park.

109
00:07:47,675 --> 00:07:52,180
Eun Chae, I'm out with the CEO.

110
00:07:52,180 --> 00:07:56,559
It'll be past 9:00 PM when we're done,
so report to me if anything comes up.

111
00:07:56,559 --> 00:07:58,502
Yes, I understand.

112
00:08:01,480 --> 00:08:04,901
So he won't be back till late?

113
00:08:04,901 --> 00:08:07,607
<i>Looks like I can make the show tonight.</i>

114
00:08:25,630 --> 00:08:29,223
Watch where you're going!
You scared me half to death!

115
00:08:30,259 --> 00:08:31,510
Excuse you.

116
00:08:31,510 --> 00:08:35,342
You're the one who should be careful
on a street like this, not me.

117
00:08:36,766 --> 00:08:38,351
This was expensive.

118
00:08:38,351 --> 00:08:40,144
Let me take you to the hospital.

119
00:08:40,144 --> 00:08:42,647
I'm fine. Just go.

120
00:08:42,647 --> 00:08:44,569
Just be careful next time.

121
00:08:45,354 --> 00:08:46,359
Just go?

122
00:08:46,359 --> 00:08:49,975
No way.
What if you report me for a hit-and-run later?

123
00:08:51,906 --> 00:08:54,367
Give me your phone. I'll put my number in.

124
00:08:54,367 --> 00:08:55,585
Your number?

125
00:08:58,238 --> 00:09:00,490
Is this how you hit on people?

126
00:09:02,458 --> 00:09:05,002
Well, if that's what you think,
I'll just leave.

127
00:09:05,002 --> 00:09:06,280
Goodbye.

128
00:09:06,280 --> 00:09:07,856
No, give it to me!

129
00:09:09,340 --> 00:09:10,967
Give it to me!

130
00:09:10,967 --> 00:09:12,396
Your number.

131
00:09:26,816 --> 00:09:29,365
Drive carefully next time. Seriously.

132
00:09:37,482 --> 00:09:40,162
Next, we'll discuss what sets OYES apart.

133
00:09:40,162 --> 00:09:43,416
First, a diversified artist portfolio.

134
00:09:43,416 --> 00:09:49,005
We mitigate risk with a balanced lineup
of singers, actors, and creators.

135
00:09:49,005 --> 00:09:52,565
Second, our in-house
content production capabilities.

136
00:09:54,385 --> 00:09:56,042
Okay.

137
00:09:57,431 --> 00:10:00,287
Time to clock out.

138
00:10:06,603 --> 00:10:09,736
<i>Don't even think about leaving. Keep working.</i>

139
00:10:12,236 --> 00:10:15,519
He's a mind reader.
Is he watching me or something?

140
00:10:18,784 --> 00:10:20,817
<i>Of course. I'm working.</i>

141
00:10:22,121 --> 00:10:23,539
Too bad, though.

142
00:10:23,539 --> 00:10:25,592
I'm stepping out for a bit.

143
00:10:34,200 --> 00:10:37,787
<i>Then go to my room
and open the last drawer on the right.</i>

144
00:10:37,787 --> 00:10:39,138
<i>What's in there?</i>

145
00:10:39,138 --> 00:10:40,848
Ugh.

146
00:10:40,848 --> 00:10:42,308
Seriously.

147
00:10:43,851 --> 00:10:46,436
The last drawer on the right.

148
00:10:50,521 --> 00:10:52,217
<i>It's locked.</i>

149
00:10:52,821 --> 00:10:54,612
<i>Correct.</i>

150
00:10:54,612 --> 00:10:56,295
What in the...

151
00:10:56,921 --> 00:10:58,433
<i>Stand by.</i>

152
00:11:03,564 --> 00:11:06,709
<i>Now, open the first drawer on the left.</i>

153
00:11:12,066 --> 00:11:14,380
<i>This one's locked too.</i>

154
00:11:14,380 --> 00:11:16,064
<i>Correct.</i>

155
00:11:29,397 --> 00:11:32,157
Forget it, forget it, forget it!

156
00:11:42,368 --> 00:11:43,934
Wait a second...

157
00:11:57,977 --> 00:12:01,049
<i>Open the closet by the window. What's in there?</i>

158
00:12:02,004 --> 00:12:03,664
<i>A shirt.</i>

159
00:12:07,594 --> 00:12:08,945
<i>Correct.</i>

160
00:12:09,520 --> 00:12:10,938
<i>Let's see.</i>

161
00:12:12,022 --> 00:12:13,272
<i>Here.</i>

162
00:12:16,902 --> 00:12:18,444
Perfect.

163
00:12:49,101 --> 00:12:51,937
<i>I'll be back after dinner.</i>

164
00:12:59,836 --> 00:13:01,874
[Donghun Chicken, Hongdae Branch]

165
00:13:08,120 --> 00:13:09,789
Step on it.

166
00:13:09,789 --> 00:13:11,499
To Hongdae.

167
00:13:43,614 --> 00:13:45,199
I'll be going now.

168
00:13:45,199 --> 00:13:46,992
Pardon?

169
00:13:46,992 --> 00:13:48,494
Sir!

170
00:13:51,455 --> 00:13:52,957
Sir.

171
00:13:52,957 --> 00:13:54,335
Sir!

172
00:14:22,653 --> 00:14:24,816
We're India Red!

173
00:14:24,816 --> 00:14:25,823
Thank you!

174
00:14:25,823 --> 00:14:28,075
Make some noise!

175
00:14:36,375 --> 00:14:39,503
Wow, how many times did he call?

176
00:14:40,588 --> 00:14:42,631
Is the music too loud?

177
00:14:47,761 --> 00:14:49,513
Don't be scared.

178
00:14:49,513 --> 00:14:51,501
I just came out for dinner.

179
00:14:57,184 --> 00:14:58,344
<i>Where are you?</i>

180
00:14:59,148 --> 00:15:00,858
Where do you think?

181
00:15:00,858 --> 00:15:02,776
Didn't you see the photo?

182
00:15:02,776 --> 00:15:04,445
I'm out for dinner.

183
00:15:04,445 --> 00:15:05,761
Are you in the office?

184
00:15:06,322 --> 00:15:08,032
You came out for dinner?

185
00:15:08,032 --> 00:15:09,404
What did you eat?

186
00:15:15,039 --> 00:15:16,873
You really came.

187
00:15:19,853 --> 00:15:21,459
<i>I didn't take off my makeup.</i>

188
00:15:31,847 --> 00:15:33,227
Well...

189
00:15:34,808 --> 00:15:39,313
I wasn't trying to fool you.

190
00:15:39,313 --> 00:15:41,031
You? Fool me?

191
00:15:46,945 --> 00:15:48,322
Fine!

192
00:15:48,322 --> 00:15:49,990
I'm Soo!

193
00:15:49,990 --> 00:15:53,202
So what? What are you going to do about it?

194
00:15:53,202 --> 00:15:54,359
By the way,

195
00:15:54,954 --> 00:15:57,296
why do you want to meet Soo so badly?

196
00:15:58,082 --> 00:16:00,209
You said you'd tell Soo yourself.

197
00:16:00,209 --> 00:16:04,197
Now that you know I'm Soo,
go ahead and tell me.

198
00:16:09,301 --> 00:16:13,430
Does a man need a reason
to want to meet a woman?

199
00:16:13,430 --> 00:16:17,626
But now that I know Soo is you, Lee Eun Chae,

200
00:16:19,144 --> 00:16:21,480
focus only on work for the next three months.

201
00:16:21,480 --> 00:16:23,857
100,000 won a day. 30 days, three million.

202
00:16:23,857 --> 00:16:25,901
Three months, nine million.

203
00:16:25,901 --> 00:16:28,529
Plus another million,
and that's exactly ten million.

204
00:16:28,529 --> 00:16:30,614
Don't I get any days off?

205
00:16:30,614 --> 00:16:33,867
You're such a labor-law-breaking slave driver.

206
00:16:33,867 --> 00:16:37,287
Then pay triple the penalty
and end the contract.

207
00:16:37,287 --> 00:16:40,457
The club looked packed earlier.

208
00:16:40,457 --> 00:16:41,959
I think you can afford it.

209
00:16:41,959 --> 00:16:44,294
You're so petty.

210
00:16:44,294 --> 00:16:47,922
How would an indie band singer
have that kind of money?

211
00:16:50,008 --> 00:16:51,552
Better yet,

212
00:16:51,552 --> 00:16:55,264
how about living together for three days
instead of a three-month contract?

213
00:16:55,264 --> 00:16:59,685
If you don't lay a finger on me
for three days, you win.

214
00:16:59,685 --> 00:17:04,444
If I win, clear the ten million
and apologize to me on top of it.

215
00:17:05,816 --> 00:17:09,653
This is why your father
keeps the hair clippers ready.

216
00:17:12,656 --> 00:17:14,301
Besides,

217
00:17:14,301 --> 00:17:17,745
living together makes the game too easy.

218
00:17:17,745 --> 00:17:21,373
Easy games bore me.
It'd be like shooting fish in a barrel.

219
00:17:21,373 --> 00:17:24,846
I'm saying I won't fall for you
even if we live together.

220
00:17:25,753 --> 00:17:28,338
That bet still stands, right?

221
00:17:28,338 --> 00:17:31,410
If I don't fall for you,

222
00:17:33,372 --> 00:17:35,387
you'll give me what I want.

223
00:17:35,387 --> 00:17:38,599
If you fall for me, you give me what I want.

224
00:17:41,310 --> 00:17:44,271
Contracts are made to be kept.

225
00:17:44,271 --> 00:17:45,314
Deal?

226
00:17:45,314 --> 00:17:46,471
Deal!

227
00:18:05,542 --> 00:18:08,212
<i>That bet still stands, right?</i>

228
00:18:08,212 --> 00:18:12,257
<i>If I don't fall for you,</i>

229
00:18:12,257 --> 00:18:14,092
<i>you'll give me what I want.</i>

230
00:18:14,092 --> 00:18:17,554
<i>If you fall for me, you give me what I want.</i>

231
00:18:17,554 --> 00:18:20,307
I need to win this bet.

232
00:18:20,307 --> 00:18:23,101
Then I can get rid of Soo.

233
00:18:29,858 --> 00:18:33,544
<i>I'm saying I won't fall for you
even if we live together.</i>

234
00:18:35,447 --> 00:18:36,698
Unbelievable.

235
00:18:36,698 --> 00:18:39,154
How can she be so confident?

236
00:18:43,413 --> 00:18:45,332
But...

237
00:18:45,332 --> 00:18:48,794
I've shown her everything.
What more could she want?

238
00:18:55,717 --> 00:18:58,095
- Theo.
<i>- Yes, boss.</i>

239
00:18:58,095 --> 00:19:01,557
I need data on the kind of men women fall for.

240
00:19:01,557 --> 00:19:05,310
Well, I'm sure I'm perfect
according to the data.

241
00:19:05,310 --> 00:19:08,062
<i>You are perfect on paper, boss, but...</i>

242
00:19:08,062 --> 00:19:09,062
But?

243
00:19:09,062 --> 00:19:10,856
<i>Women want attention to detail.</i>

244
00:19:10,856 --> 00:19:13,986
<i>Like a surprise gift just for her.</i>

245
00:19:13,986 --> 00:19:16,166
So it's about money after all.

246
00:19:21,034 --> 00:19:23,320
<i>But it's not just about the money.</i>

247
00:19:33,088 --> 00:19:36,819
<i>Come here. 1st floor, 345 Cheongdam-dong.</i>

248
00:19:46,220 --> 00:19:49,795
345 Cheongdam-dong, 1st floor.

249
00:19:50,397 --> 00:19:51,857
This is the place.

250
00:19:52,441 --> 00:19:55,235
What is he up to now?

251
00:20:17,551 --> 00:20:19,512
Hello.

252
00:20:20,844 --> 00:20:23,639
I'm here to see someone.

253
00:20:23,639 --> 00:20:25,307
This way, please.

254
00:20:35,248 --> 00:20:37,986
It's my lunch break.
Why did you call me out here?

255
00:20:37,986 --> 00:20:39,154
And...

256
00:20:39,154 --> 00:20:41,782
why come here
when you've got no woman to buy for?

257
00:20:41,782 --> 00:20:46,186
Whether I do or not isn't something you'd know.

258
00:21:06,932 --> 00:21:08,350
Want me to buy it for you?

259
00:21:08,350 --> 00:21:11,214
<i>Really? How much is it?</i>

260
00:21:11,214 --> 00:21:13,730
[9.5 million won]

261
00:21:13,730 --> 00:21:15,232
<i>Holy cow!</i>

262
00:21:15,232 --> 00:21:17,818
<i>No, Lee Eun Chae. Get a grip.</i>

263
00:21:17,818 --> 00:21:20,184
<i>There's no such thing as a free lunch.</i>

264
00:21:20,904 --> 00:21:22,239
No, forget it.

265
00:21:22,239 --> 00:21:23,349
I don't need it.

266
00:21:23,349 --> 00:21:25,075
Think of it as a gift.

267
00:21:25,075 --> 00:21:27,703
Don't women love getting gifts?

268
00:21:27,703 --> 00:21:29,830
- Wrap it up, please.
- Yes, sir.

269
00:21:29,830 --> 00:21:31,498
<i>No, get a grip.</i>

270
00:21:31,498 --> 00:21:33,000
<i>He's just playing games.</i>

271
00:21:33,000 --> 00:21:34,501
No, forget it.

272
00:21:35,460 --> 00:21:37,713
I said I'm fine. I don't need it.

273
00:21:37,713 --> 00:21:40,048
If you don't need it, take it and toss it.

274
00:21:40,048 --> 00:21:42,264
I want to give it to you anyway.

275
00:21:43,885 --> 00:21:45,804
Don't try to bait me like this.

276
00:21:45,804 --> 00:21:48,325
It only makes me dislike you more.

277
00:21:59,651 --> 00:22:01,653
The data was wrong.

278
00:22:01,653 --> 00:22:03,817
<i>Look in the mirror, boss.</i>

279
00:22:06,925 --> 00:22:07,951
What do you mean?

280
00:22:07,951 --> 00:22:11,299
<i>Here are the moments women fall for men.</i>

281
00:22:13,979 --> 00:22:16,207
[Moments when a woman falls for a man]

282
00:22:16,835 --> 00:22:19,825
Do they really fall for things like this?

283
00:22:21,757 --> 00:22:23,033
Why?

284
00:22:54,581 --> 00:22:58,743
<i>When he unbuttons his white shirt,
rolls up his sleeves, and focuses on work.</i>

285
00:23:09,888 --> 00:23:11,788
You're not sick, are you?

286
00:23:12,599 --> 00:23:14,434
What?

287
00:23:16,353 --> 00:23:18,438
I don't like where this is.

288
00:23:18,438 --> 00:23:20,012
It needs to move.

289
00:23:23,193 --> 00:23:27,643
<i>When she sees the veins pop on his forearms
as he moves something heavy.</i>

290
00:23:28,657 --> 00:23:31,087
<i>She looks smitten already.</i>

291
00:23:36,748 --> 00:23:39,668
I think the original spot was better.

292
00:23:39,668 --> 00:23:40,752
Really?

293
00:23:44,528 --> 00:23:46,701
How about here?

294
00:23:57,894 --> 00:23:59,787
<i>When he pats her on the head.</i>

295
00:24:00,777 --> 00:24:02,653
<i>A head pat?</i>

296
00:24:06,778 --> 00:24:08,113
<i>It means stroking someone,</i>

297
00:24:08,113 --> 00:24:13,493
<i>the way an owner shows affection
by petting a dog or a cat.</i>

298
00:24:13,493 --> 00:24:15,912
<i>Time for the finishing touch.</i>

299
00:24:15,912 --> 00:24:17,336
There, there.

300
00:24:22,627 --> 00:24:24,192
What was that?

301
00:24:24,963 --> 00:24:26,423
Well...

302
00:24:27,591 --> 00:24:31,303
Why are you touching my hair?
Why did you mess it up?

303
00:24:31,303 --> 00:24:34,472
Ugh, this took more effort than you'd think!

304
00:24:34,472 --> 00:24:36,654
You're such a weirdo!

305
00:24:41,897 --> 00:24:45,358
Is this a data error? Or...

306
00:24:45,358 --> 00:24:48,316
is Lee Eun Chae the error in the data?

307
00:25:01,594 --> 00:25:02,980
What are you doing?

308
00:25:04,294 --> 00:25:07,464
You're throwing this away, right?

309
00:25:07,464 --> 00:25:09,674
Well, yes, but...

310
00:25:09,674 --> 00:25:12,177
Then mind if I listen to it?

311
00:25:13,470 --> 00:25:15,408
Did the CEO ask for it?

312
00:25:16,556 --> 00:25:19,142
So what's going on with you and the CEO?

313
00:25:19,142 --> 00:25:21,895
He's the CEO, and I'm his secretary.

314
00:25:21,895 --> 00:25:25,083
It's just... I saw you two
come in together that morning.

315
00:25:26,358 --> 00:25:28,902
We just had breakfast together.

316
00:25:28,902 --> 00:25:30,070
Is that a problem?

317
00:25:30,070 --> 00:25:32,115
No, not at all.

318
00:25:33,065 --> 00:25:34,795
What's going on?

319
00:25:34,795 --> 00:25:36,560
It's nothing, Director Oh.

320
00:25:37,244 --> 00:25:40,288
The CEO's new secretary.
Must have pulled some strings.

321
00:25:40,288 --> 00:25:43,458
She had breakfast with the CEO
and came in with him.

322
00:25:43,458 --> 00:25:46,503
Do secretaries usually
have breakfast with their bosses?

323
00:25:46,503 --> 00:25:48,838
So they must have met at dawn, right?

324
00:25:48,838 --> 00:25:50,732
Isn't it strange?

325
00:25:53,843 --> 00:25:56,709
Can't believe she's saying that
loud enough for me to hear.

326
00:26:14,322 --> 00:26:17,325
You're working harder than I expected.

327
00:26:17,325 --> 00:26:20,959
If you're cut out for this business,
you could stay for good.

328
00:26:28,155 --> 00:26:30,201
Am I talking to myself?

329
00:26:36,011 --> 00:26:38,013
What now? What?

330
00:26:38,013 --> 00:26:39,931
Here to listen to music? Go home.

331
00:26:39,931 --> 00:26:41,099
Really?

332
00:26:41,099 --> 00:26:42,767
I mean straight home.

333
00:26:42,767 --> 00:26:45,265
Don't lie and sneak off somewhere else.

334
00:26:48,064 --> 00:26:51,186
Has he been possessed by my dad or something?

335
00:26:52,777 --> 00:26:54,466
Forget it. I'll take you.

336
00:26:54,988 --> 00:26:56,531
No, thanks.

337
00:26:56,531 --> 00:27:01,202
The staff already saw us
come in together the other day.

338
00:27:01,202 --> 00:27:03,538
Who knows what rumors will start this time?

339
00:27:03,538 --> 00:27:05,623
We've got nothing to hide.

340
00:27:05,623 --> 00:27:07,625
Just tell them it's not true.

341
00:27:07,625 --> 00:27:09,909
You argue with me just fine.

342
00:27:12,633 --> 00:27:15,215
When I say I'm taking you, I'm taking you.

343
00:27:16,593 --> 00:27:19,846
You've been really weird lately, you know that?

344
00:27:19,846 --> 00:27:22,968
Fine, let's go.

345
00:27:24,559 --> 00:27:28,146
But I'm going home alone today.

346
00:27:28,146 --> 00:27:30,367
You're such a weirdo.

347
00:27:32,953 --> 00:27:34,426
Happy clocking out!

348
00:27:37,030 --> 00:27:39,476
Go straight home! No detours!

349
00:27:42,744 --> 00:27:46,117
Why am I acting like this?

350
00:28:06,051 --> 00:28:07,352
Do Hyeok, you're here.

351
00:28:07,352 --> 00:28:09,020
Yes.

352
00:28:09,020 --> 00:28:10,647
So why did you want me here?

353
00:28:11,825 --> 00:28:14,476
To take a family photo.

354
00:28:19,781 --> 00:28:23,034
Didn't the chairman tell you?

355
00:28:23,034 --> 00:28:25,913
He only said to stop by before going to work.

356
00:28:27,428 --> 00:28:29,833
Honestly, that man.

357
00:28:29,833 --> 00:28:33,420
Well, at least your work clothes
will do for the photo.

358
00:28:33,420 --> 00:28:37,465
Mr. Park, the chairman is outside.
Please bring him in.

359
00:28:37,465 --> 00:28:39,467
- Yes, ma'am.
- Do Yeon.

360
00:28:39,467 --> 00:28:42,218
Gosh, what's taking her? Do Yeon.

361
00:28:44,556 --> 00:28:45,880
I'll go.

362
00:28:56,901 --> 00:28:58,736
I'm not taking the photo.

363
00:28:58,736 --> 00:29:01,156
This isn't like you. What's all this about?

364
00:29:01,156 --> 00:29:05,076
Your stepmother wants it so badly.
Just go along with it.

365
00:29:05,076 --> 00:29:06,411
I...

366
00:29:06,411 --> 00:29:08,455
I'm doing everything you ask of me,

367
00:29:08,455 --> 00:29:11,916
but I don't want my face hanging
in this house as part of the family.

368
00:29:11,916 --> 00:29:14,627
Your denial doesn't change
the fact that we're family.

369
00:29:14,627 --> 00:29:15,879
Right.

370
00:29:15,879 --> 00:29:18,840
Just like how Mom's death doesn't disappear

371
00:29:18,840 --> 00:29:22,260
even if you burned everything
that belonged to her.

372
00:29:22,260 --> 00:29:23,809
Isn't that right?

373
00:29:24,429 --> 00:29:27,140
Everyone does what they must to survive.

374
00:29:27,140 --> 00:29:30,393
Especially when money and power are involved.

375
00:29:30,393 --> 00:29:32,353
Your stepmother

376
00:29:32,353 --> 00:29:34,564
is doing that to survive, too.

377
00:29:34,564 --> 00:29:35,857
And

378
00:29:35,857 --> 00:29:38,026
this isn't the time

379
00:29:38,026 --> 00:29:41,051
to flaunt your petty pride in front of me.

380
00:29:45,158 --> 00:29:47,118
Yes, we're ready.

381
00:29:47,118 --> 00:29:48,870
Let's get started!

382
00:29:48,870 --> 00:29:50,830
Just relax and look at the lens.

383
00:29:50,830 --> 00:29:53,208
You can rest a hand there, like that.

384
00:29:53,208 --> 00:29:57,046
Let's take the shot. One, two, three!

385
00:29:59,452 --> 00:30:00,840
Ouch...

386
00:30:00,840 --> 00:30:02,258
What do we do?

387
00:30:02,258 --> 00:30:04,511
Jin Woo, I think you should carry him.

388
00:30:04,511 --> 00:30:07,305
- Me?
- No! He'll hurt his back.

389
00:30:07,305 --> 00:30:09,140
The three of us can lift him.

390
00:30:09,140 --> 00:30:11,559
- Okay, okay. Father.
- Hold him.

391
00:30:11,559 --> 00:30:12,852
Father, lean back.

392
00:30:12,852 --> 00:30:14,521
- Grab his legs.
- The legs.

393
00:30:14,521 --> 00:30:16,689
Okay, slowly, slowly.

394
00:30:16,689 --> 00:30:18,879
One, two, three!

395
00:30:21,861 --> 00:30:23,071
Honey, are you okay?

396
00:30:23,071 --> 00:30:24,697
Honey, are you all right?

397
00:30:24,697 --> 00:30:26,324
Dad!

398
00:30:28,581 --> 00:30:30,973
I'll... I'll walk. I can do it.

399
00:30:30,973 --> 00:30:32,956
- I will.
- No, Father.

400
00:30:32,956 --> 00:30:35,413
- Are you okay? Careful.
- Father, I'm the doctor.

401
00:30:35,413 --> 00:30:37,040
- Be careful.
- Father.

402
00:30:37,040 --> 00:30:38,620
Just trust me.

403
00:30:45,593 --> 00:30:48,304
Eun Chae's father is unwell
and in the hospital.

404
00:30:48,304 --> 00:30:51,185
I'll make sure it doesn't affect your schedule.

405
00:30:58,332 --> 00:31:00,265
<i>What's going on?</i>

406
00:31:00,265 --> 00:31:03,232
<i>My father hurt his back and is in the hospital.</i>

407
00:31:03,232 --> 00:31:06,131
<i>It can't be helped today, so cut me some slack.</i>

408
00:31:06,964 --> 00:31:08,405
<i>Which hospital?</i>

409
00:31:09,067 --> 00:31:12,161
<i>Why? Are you going to visit him?</i>

410
00:31:12,161 --> 00:31:13,496
Why?

411
00:31:13,496 --> 00:31:15,960
Are you going to visit him?

412
00:31:17,500 --> 00:31:18,960
<i>No.</i>

413
00:31:18,960 --> 00:31:21,050
<i>Just checking if you were lying.</i>

414
00:31:29,178 --> 00:31:30,847
Dad, are you okay?

415
00:31:30,847 --> 00:31:32,932
Eun Chae.

416
00:31:32,932 --> 00:31:35,560
Bring the album when you come.

417
00:31:35,560 --> 00:31:39,147
What? Is there a song you want to hear?

418
00:31:39,147 --> 00:31:41,232
The family album.

419
00:31:42,609 --> 00:31:44,444
Why the family album?

420
00:31:44,444 --> 00:31:47,447
I'm having surgery.

421
00:31:47,447 --> 00:31:50,116
I might never see you all again.

422
00:31:50,116 --> 00:31:54,495
Come on Dad. Don't say things like that.

423
00:31:54,495 --> 00:31:59,542
I have to see you get married before I go.

424
00:31:59,542 --> 00:32:02,086
Dad.

425
00:32:02,086 --> 00:32:05,154
Why? Did the doctor say it's serious?

426
00:32:06,132 --> 00:32:07,592
Gosh.

427
00:32:07,592 --> 00:32:09,802
I heard it's just disc surgery.

428
00:32:09,802 --> 00:32:13,419
You're acting like it's a funeral.

429
00:32:18,561 --> 00:32:20,301
Don't laugh, you punk.

430
00:32:21,542 --> 00:32:23,568
Make sure to bring that album.

431
00:32:24,359 --> 00:32:27,341
Okay, okay, I will.

432
00:32:45,797 --> 00:32:50,604
You've made a habit of not replying.

433
00:32:50,604 --> 00:32:52,238
Aren't there any decent men at work?

434
00:32:52,238 --> 00:32:54,111
Not at all.

435
00:32:54,889 --> 00:32:56,766
Eun Chae, do you want a blind date?

436
00:32:56,766 --> 00:32:58,518
A blind date?

437
00:32:58,518 --> 00:33:00,900
If he's like you, Jin Woo, sure.

438
00:33:01,396 --> 00:33:04,023
My sister really lucked out.

439
00:33:04,023 --> 00:33:05,066
She did.

440
00:33:05,066 --> 00:33:06,451
That's a fact.

441
00:33:15,493 --> 00:33:17,286
<i>Don't tell Eun Seo.</i>

442
00:33:17,286 --> 00:33:18,286
<i>Got it?</i>

443
00:33:30,341 --> 00:33:32,802
- Looking for Jin Woo?
- Yeah.

444
00:33:32,802 --> 00:33:36,097
He must have left his phone in his office.

445
00:33:36,097 --> 00:33:38,182
- Really?
- Yeah.

446
00:33:38,182 --> 00:33:39,726
I'll go look for it.

447
00:33:39,726 --> 00:33:41,144
What?

448
00:33:41,144 --> 00:33:43,479
Go wait in the basement cafe for now, okay?

449
00:33:43,479 --> 00:33:44,480
Wait.

450
00:33:46,524 --> 00:33:49,235
The cafe. Got it? I'm off.

451
00:33:49,235 --> 00:33:50,939
What's with him?

452
00:33:52,238 --> 00:33:55,032
- Everything okay with Father?
- Hello.

453
00:33:55,032 --> 00:33:56,159
Jin Woo.

454
00:33:56,159 --> 00:33:57,910
Eun Seo is here.

455
00:33:57,910 --> 00:33:59,079
Eun Seo?

456
00:34:04,751 --> 00:34:06,511
<i>No wonder he's startled.</i>

457
00:34:08,504 --> 00:34:10,256
But Tae Gyeong...

458
00:34:10,256 --> 00:34:12,592
<i>What's with that look? Don't tell me...</i>

459
00:34:12,592 --> 00:34:14,927
<i>Are you two really seeing each other?</i>

460
00:34:14,927 --> 00:34:18,139
No, Jin Woo. Let's talk later.
Hurry and go see Eun Seo.

461
00:34:18,139 --> 00:34:19,432
- No.
- What?

462
00:34:19,432 --> 00:34:22,894
- At least say hello before you go.
- Say hello?

463
00:34:22,894 --> 00:34:24,228
Say hello.

464
00:34:24,228 --> 00:34:27,447
This is Moon Tae Gyeong,
a junior of mine from Pediatrics.

465
00:34:32,862 --> 00:34:35,114
- The social worker?
- Yes.

466
00:34:35,114 --> 00:34:37,283
- We meet again.
- What?

467
00:34:37,283 --> 00:34:39,600
Have you two met before?

468
00:34:42,246 --> 00:34:45,369
Jin Woo. He caught me.

469
00:34:46,959 --> 00:34:48,920
Wait... you two are family?

470
00:34:48,920 --> 00:34:49,920
Yeah.

471
00:34:50,490 --> 00:34:52,192
This is my sister-in-law.

472
00:34:54,675 --> 00:34:56,673
Eun Seo's sister.

473
00:35:00,473 --> 00:35:03,434
So that's why you had me get her a bouquet?

474
00:35:03,434 --> 00:35:06,994
So that's why you gave me those flowers.

475
00:35:15,488 --> 00:35:16,989
Thank you.

476
00:35:27,416 --> 00:35:31,752
I really thought you were a fan.

477
00:35:32,266 --> 00:35:34,757
So it was Jin Woo's request.

478
00:35:34,757 --> 00:35:36,717
Well, I'm a fan now.

479
00:35:36,717 --> 00:35:40,471
You're Eun Seo's sister? Wow, I had no idea.

480
00:35:40,471 --> 00:35:42,009
You don't look alike at all.

481
00:35:42,009 --> 00:35:43,291
Not at all.

482
00:35:44,725 --> 00:35:46,727
Eun Seo doesn't know, does she?

483
00:35:46,727 --> 00:35:51,065
Only Jin Woo knew,

484
00:35:51,065 --> 00:35:53,994
but now one more person knows.

485
00:35:57,655 --> 00:35:59,407
Don't worry.

486
00:35:59,407 --> 00:36:01,021
I'll keep it a secret.

487
00:36:03,744 --> 00:36:06,720
Next show, I'll buy them myself.

488
00:36:07,874 --> 00:36:09,125
The bouquet.

489
00:36:09,125 --> 00:36:11,043
Really?

490
00:36:11,043 --> 00:36:12,043
Yes.

491
00:36:15,673 --> 00:36:19,244
<i>Now, let's see if she looks natural
when she sings.</i>

492
00:36:23,374 --> 00:36:24,774
<i>Looks good.</i>

493
00:36:31,314 --> 00:36:33,314
<i>But you don't look too happy.</i>

494
00:36:34,275 --> 00:36:36,353
No, I'm fine.

495
00:36:37,653 --> 00:36:40,322
I just have a bit of indigestion.

496
00:36:42,617 --> 00:36:44,353
<i>But, Do Hyeok.</i>

497
00:36:56,874 --> 00:36:59,697
I wish someone would prick my finger to fix it.

498
00:37:02,055 --> 00:37:04,454
You wanted banana milk that badly?

499
00:37:05,556 --> 00:37:08,559
I might never get to drink it again.

500
00:37:08,559 --> 00:37:09,727
Gosh.

501
00:37:09,727 --> 00:37:11,177
There you go again.

502
00:37:12,146 --> 00:37:13,397
Just look at you.

503
00:37:13,397 --> 00:37:16,900
How can you be so different from Eun Seo?

504
00:37:18,152 --> 00:37:19,654
Come on.

505
00:37:19,654 --> 00:37:22,782
I've got a job, too, at a big company.

506
00:37:22,782 --> 00:37:25,076
You're just an intern.

507
00:37:25,076 --> 00:37:27,244
And you stayed out all night...

508
00:37:27,244 --> 00:37:28,633
My back.

509
00:37:29,914 --> 00:37:31,345
You punk.

510
00:37:32,052 --> 00:37:34,669
Aren't you ashamed

511
00:37:34,669 --> 00:37:37,129
to face your mother, even in a photo?

512
00:37:37,129 --> 00:37:41,400
Then I just won't look at Mom's photo.

513
00:37:41,926 --> 00:37:43,094
You little brat.

514
00:37:43,094 --> 00:37:44,761
Come here.

515
00:37:45,429 --> 00:37:48,693
Dad, stop trying to hit me! You're injured!

516
00:37:50,059 --> 00:37:54,522
Please pull yourself together
and live like everyone else.

517
00:37:54,522 --> 00:37:59,006
Then I can die in peace.

518
00:37:59,818 --> 00:38:02,196
Don't talk about dying.

519
00:38:02,196 --> 00:38:03,864
If you're that lonely,

520
00:38:03,864 --> 00:38:07,576
stop looking at Mom's photo
and just get remarried!

521
00:38:08,725 --> 00:38:13,499
It's just disc surgery,
so what's all the fighting about?

522
00:38:13,499 --> 00:38:16,085
- You don't get it, Granny!
- You don't get it, Granny!

523
00:38:19,588 --> 00:38:20,673
My back.

524
00:38:20,673 --> 00:38:22,591
I give up.

525
00:38:22,591 --> 00:38:27,138
A lifetime of banana milk
wouldn't make you appreciate me.

526
00:39:11,812 --> 00:39:15,000
